{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf-fpqc-ph-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ad05b69e4098c7f36fc841e2d7009fbca62568fa2ca3724cdee4a9c1d59886ab", "source_text": "Any fpqc covering is a V covering. A fortiori,\nany fppf, syntomic, smooth, <ACCENT_0001>tale or Zariski covering is a V covering.\nAlso, a ph covering is a V covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9ca51ff40eb507b8808d410608da3e02da4a0d26edbe3442ba4f91bd34354084", "unit_id": "tag:0ETK:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fpqc-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-standard-fpqc-standard-V}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf-fpqc}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-standard-ph-standard-V}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7e7e3d342d691871171fe38bbf868d6afa22a8c249458038cf8887f6bc3576aa", "source_text": "An fpqc covering can affine locally be refined by a\nstandard fpqc covering, see Lemmas <REF_0001>.\nA standard fpqc covering is a standard V covering, see\nLemma <REF_0002>. Hence the first statement\nfollows from our definition of V covers in terms of standard V coverings.\nThe conclusion for fppf, syntomic, smooth, <ACCENT_0001>tale or Zariski coverings\nfollows as these are fpqc coverings, see\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nThe statement on ph coverings follows from\nLemma <REF_0004> in the same manner.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:049ed654c05ca9185c095fca34407e2b1c0dead417c069ff2bb27366fda77e4f", "unit_id": "tag:0ETK:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-sheaf-property-fpqc}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-sheaf-property-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:363a290d6744accd5535fc8d500d545ef09ef038e8a60b5d39cf3873af786fdb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:40f1e18bba1814330eb6445fbcc7372921f07a893d8efaf963a79e878becf077", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a contravariant functor on the category\nof schemes with values in sets. We say that\n<MATH_0002> <TEXTITOPEN_0001>satisfies the sheaf property for the V topology<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif it satisfies the sheaf property for any V covering\n(see Definition <REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e90a815dfd2c484ddfe5b9b44b21fe7c1ae59777456f2afecb62ce1d3725665b", "unit_id": "tag:0ETL:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6247390cfab2169ec242d530b639df3a175e37efeb5d8cc6ec5f68ed55ae7def", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:72b515b203b20a6f15667ab8f25a2897e43bf6fa4c9c0a311164de8e1f19343b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe try to avoid using the terminology ``<MATH_0001> is a sheaf'' in this\nsituation since we are not defining a category of V sheaves\nas we explained above.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe72c276a2a6b4f271cfde8eacc2a13a8dd4b4679529013e7171e660ab93f359", "unit_id": "tag:0ETA:prose-0004"}
